All bands continuous; no wrong fixed amount anywhere. Duty, computing top-of-band and comparing to the next band's fixed:
  @12,000: 12,000 x 0.01 = 120 = band-2 fixed 120. OK
  @30,000: 120 + 18,000 x 0.02 = 480 = band-3 fixed 480. OK
  @50,000: 480 + 20,000 x 0.03 = 1,080 = band-4 fixed 1,080. OK
  @100,000: 1,080 + 50,000 x 0.035 = 2,830 = band-5 fixed 2,830. OK
  @200,000: 2,830 + 100,000 x 0.04 = 6,830 = band-6 fixed 6,830. OK
  @250,000: 6,830 + 50,000 x 0.0425 = 8,955 = band-7 fixed 8,955. OK
  @300,000: 8,955 + 50,000 x 0.0475 = 11,330 = band-8 fixed 11,330. OK
  @500,000: 11,330 + 200,000 x 0.05 = 21,330 = band-9 fixed 21,330. OK
Zero jumps across all 8 interior boundaries.

Land tax general:
  @936,000: nil band ends at 0; band 2 has fixed 0 and charges only above 936,000. Continuous (no cliff).
  @1,504,000: 0 + (1,504,000 - 936,000) x 0.005 = 568,000 x 0.005 = 2,840 = band-3 fixed 2,840. OK
  @2,188,000: 2,840 + 684,000 x 0.01 = 2,840 + 6,840 = 9,680 = band-4 fixed 9,680. OK
  @3,504,000: 9,680 + 1,316,000 x 0.02 = 9,680 + 26,320 = 36,000 = band-5 fixed 36,000. OK

Trust scale (in landTaxSurcharges):
  @25,000: deliberate cliff — Nil below, then $125 fixed. 25,000 x 0.005 = 125, i.e. the fixed is exactly a clawback of the threshold, so the scale is continuous with a notional 0.5%-from-zero line. Published as-is; correctly transcribed.
  @936,000: 125 + 911,000 x 0.005 = 125 + 4,555 = 4,680 = next fixed 4,680. OK
  @1,504,000: 4,680 + 568,000 x 0.01 = 4,680 + 5,680 = 10,360 = next fixed 10,360. OK
  @2,188,000: 10,360 + 684,000 x 0.015 = 10,360 + 10,260 = 20,620 = next fixed 20,620. OK
  @3,504,000: 20,620 + 1,316,000 x 0.024 = 20,620 + 31,584 = 52,204 = next fixed 52,204. OK
Note the trust top boundary at $3,504,000 is arithmetically redundant (2.40% both sides) but that redundancy is present in RevenueSA's published table, so transcribing it is faithful, not an error.
